    "Existing detached allocation owns free/oldest/sentinel cases, owner selection, one-use funding and packet21/151/owner publication. No new item writer or RNG stream.",
    "Source capability, player/owner/calendar/RNG/clock/retained footprint guards finish before callback-free item adoption and shared RNG commit; publication follows.",
    "Existing authenticated command59/bootstrap and two outbound endpoint projections receive item birth before switch relay. All three statues are exercised by the existing shipping WiringNativeSmoke path."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "NPC statues, King/Queen town teleports, arbitrary wet or actuated statue footprints and wider wiring/client acceptance remain open; issue125 is not closed.",
    "Canonical source traces have no active players and compare original full physical item/RNG/cooldown state plus packet21/151 bytes. Controlled stock clearing and physical ages are explicit inputs; only mechanism clocks advance, not item physics or Main.Update.",
    "Authenticated endpoint/funding tests are in-process authority/queue projections, not a newly captured unmodified GUI or real TCP-client playthrough. Existing ordinary pickup owners are reused; no direct inventory credit is granted.",
    "Heart/star require an owned calendar and all births require the existing qualified source RNG and item-owner facts. Unknown dependencies and protected transient allocations refuse without speculative item/RNG adoption.",
    "Source cooldown registration precedes population/birth checks and is retained when the subsequent allocation or owner transaction refuses.",
    "Local NativeAOT and system C++ installation remain user-deferred. Previous mainCI43813502610 Windows/LinuxNative and CoreCLR jobs succeeded; new local native acceptance is not asserted.",
    "Issue126 still awaits absent affected/unaffected connection stop logs; no timeout/abuse policy was loosened."
